 We need to determine the equation for $-$ $\Delta H^{\ominus}$ (formation) of $\mathrm{DyCl}_3(\mathrm{~s})$.

\begin{aligned}
\mathrm{DyCl}_3(\mathrm{~s}) \rightarrow \mathrm{DyCl}_3(\mathrm{~aq}), & \Delta H^{\ominus} = -180.06 \mathrm{~kJ/mol} \\
\mathrm{Dy}(\mathrm{s})+3 \mathrm{HCl}(\mathrm{aq}, 4.0 \mathrm{~M}) \rightarrow \mathrm{DyCl}_3(\mathrm{aq}), & \Delta H^{\ominus} = -699.43 \mathrm{~kJ/mol} \\
\frac{1}{2} \mathrm{H}_2(\mathrm{~g})+\frac{1}{2} \mathrm{Cl}_2(\mathrm{~g}) \rightarrow \mathrm{HCl}(\mathrm{aq}, 4.0 \mathrm{M}), & \Delta H^{\ominus} = -158.31 \mathrm{~kJ/mol} \\
\end{aligned}

Using Hess's Law, we have:

$\Delta H^{\ominus}(\mathrm{DyCl}_3(\mathrm{~s}))=\Delta H_1+\Delta H_2-3 \times \Delta H_3$ [Multiply $\Delta H_3$ by 3, since 3 moles of $\mathrm{HCl}$ have been produced.]

Using the given values, we get:

\begin{aligned}
\Delta H^{\ominus}(\mathrm{DyCl}_3(\mathrm{~s}))=(-180.06)+(-699.43)+3(158.31) &= -750.6 \mathrm{~kJ} \mathrm{~mol}^{-1} \\
\end{aligned}

The answer is (A). -750.6 kJ mol−1
